\begin{cases}
a(1)^2 + b(1) + c = 1 \\
a(2)^2 + b(2) + c = 3 \\
a(3)^2 + b(3) + c = 2
\end{cases}
\] This simplifies to: \[
\begin{cases}
a + b + c = 1 \\
4a + 2b + c = 3 \\
9a + 3b + c = 2
\end{cases}
\] We can solve this system of equations. Subtract the first equation from the second and the second equation from the third to eliminate \( c \): \[
\begin{cases}
(4a + 2b + c) - (a + b + c) = 3 - 1 \Rightarrow 3a + b = 2 \\
(9a + 3b + c) - (4a + 2b + c) = 2 - 3 \Rightarrow 5a + b = -1
\end{cases}
\] Subtract the first new equation from the second to eliminate \( b \): \[
(5a + b) - (3a + b) = -1 - 2 \Rightarrow 2a = -3 \Rightarrow a = -\frac{3}{2}
\] Substitute \( a = -\frac{3}{2} \) back into \( 3a + b = 2 \): \[
3 \left( -\frac{3}{2} \right) + b = 2 \Rightarrow -\frac{9}{2} + b = 2 \Rightarrow b = 2 + \frac{9}{2} = \frac{13}{2}
\] Substitute \( a = -\frac{3}{2} \) and \( b = \frac{13}{2} \) back into \( a + b + c = 1 \): \[
-\frac{3}{2} + \frac{13}{2} + c = 1 \Rightarrow \frac{10}{2} + c = 1 \Rightarrow 5 + c = 1 \Rightarrow c = -4
\] So the polynomial is \( p(x) = -\frac{3}{2} x^2 + \frac{13}{2} x - 4 \). </think> <answer> \frac{3 + \sqrt{5}}{2} </answer>

